<!--
    Synopsys ARCv2 (specs/Ghidra/Processors/ARC), kuna #1632.  Three functions
    compiled by `arc-zephyr-elf-gcc -mcpu=em4 -O2` and linked at 0x1000.

    sum   - a zero-overhead loop: `mov lp_count,r2 ; lp 0x102a ; ld.aw ; add_s`.
            `lp` writes the loop start into the decode context of the address it
            names as the loop end, and the instruction decoded there carries the
            hardware's end-of-body test, a direct branch back.  The loop is a
            `do .. while`, counted by lp_count.
    fill  - the loop ends on a call (`bl.d sink` at 0x104c), whose delay slot
            loads the argument; the call still has one callee and the frame
            array is recovered.
    clamp - a long immediate after the instruction word, `brlo`, and a delay
            slot on each return.

    Stage: 01 decode / 02 P-code lift (a new SLEIGH language).  No option: the
    language is selected by the image's machine and is inert everywhere else.
-->
